    <string name="cpu_gpu_reads_long_prompts_chat_history_and_images_faster_on_the_gpu_and_us">"CPU + GPU reads long prompts, chat history and images faster on the GPU and uses a little more memory. Answers are written by the CPU either way."</string>
    <string name="auto_sizes_the_window_from_free_memory_at_load_without_taking_the_expert_ca">"Auto sizes the window from free memory at load, without taking the expert cache a large model needs for its speed."</string>
    <string name="max_loads_the_model_s_full_trained_length_or_as_much_as_free_memory_allows">"Max loads the model\'s full trained length, or as much as free memory allows. Large models then keep a smaller expert cache and answer more slowly."</string>
    <string name="the_window_grows_for_longer_messages_and_attachments_when_memory_allows_the">" The window grows for longer messages and attachments when memory allows; the circle beside Send shows how much of it a chat uses."</string>
    <string name="equity_runs_models_entirely_on_this_phone_prompts_answers_and_conversations">"Equity runs models entirely on this phone. Prompts, answers and conversations are never uploaded, and there are no accounts, ads or analytics. The network is used only for model downloads you start."</string>
    <string name="after_each_answer_the_model_s_state_of_this_conversation_is_saved_on_this_p">"After each answer the model\'s state of this conversation is saved on this phone. Coming back to the chat, after another chat or a restart, continues at once instead of reading the whole conversation again. It uses storage, grows with the chat and is deleted with it. A state is saved only when the model\'s next turn can continue from it; some models\' chat templates never allow that."</string>
    <string name="negative_values_remove_the_vector_s_direction_from_every_layer_1_removes_it">"Negative values remove the vector\'s direction from every layer; -1 removes it entirely. Positive values add the direction at its layer. Strength is an experimental manual setting. A steered answer is not saved as the chat\'s state."</string>
    <string name="in_developer_options_set_background_process_limit_to_no_background_processe">"In Developer options, set Background process limit to No background processes. Android then stops keeping closed apps in memory. Come back here when it is set. The limit lasts until the phone restarts; other apps start from scratch when you open them again."</string>
    <string name="developer_options_are_turned_off_open_about_phone_then_software_information">"Developer options are turned off. Open About phone, then Software information, and tap Build number seven times. Then come back and tap Free memory again."</string>
